  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 245 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nFriday into Saturday, an upper ridge translates across Texas and is \nquickly replaced by a shortwave trough, ushering in more active \nweather. Rain chances begin to increase over our westernmost \ncounties Friday afternoon, spreading eastward into Saturday. The \nbest odds for scattered to numerous showers will be west of the \nPecos River Friday evening. Otherwise, coverage looks isolated to \nscattered. Rain chances shift to the eastern half of the area \nSaturday, then tapper off over the northeastern Permian Basin Sunday \nmorning. Meanwhile, a secondary trough develops into a cut-off low \nnear the Texas Panhandle. The associated cold front is progged to \nsweep into our region Sunday afternoon into Monday. In terms of \ntemperatures, highs in the upper 60s to low 70s Friday give way to \nmainly 60s Saturday and Sunday. Highs in the 50s become more \ncommonplace behind the cold front Monday and Tuesday, then rebound \ninto the 60s Wednesday.",
